From 8b1964b10d3fa0973cebb2e0d095b2528bfd5344 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:24:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] GFDL MP v3: convert back to specific ratios on the input
 mass basis

The species enter as mixing ratios with 1/(1 - qv_in) and leave with
1/(1 + qv_new), so the host's species mass is the true mass divided by
(1 - qv_in)*(1 + r_v,new). The same defect was fixed in Thompson.

Convert back with 1/(1 - qv_in): the host keeps the input layer mass.

Measured (control_iovr4_gfdlmpv3, C96, 24 h): microphysics water residual
-8.39e-3 -> -9.3e-16 kg/m2/day (-1.03 % of its precipitation). T +0.001 K,
precipitation +0.15 %, rms 1.1-1.3x noise.

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
---
 physics/MP/GFDL/v3_2022/gfdl_cloud_microphys_v3_mod.F90 | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/physics/MP/GFDL/v3_2022/gfdl_cloud_microphys_v3_mod.F90 b/physics/MP/GFDL/v3_2022/gfdl_cloud_microphys_v3_mod.F90
index 55aaa9e0..b5c24030 100644
--- a/physics/MP/GFDL/v3_2022/gfdl_cloud_microphys_v3_mod.F90
+++ b/physics/MP/GFDL/v3_2022/gfdl_cloud_microphys_v3_mod.F90
@@ -1220,7 +1220,8 @@ subroutine mpdrv (hydrostatic, ua, va, wa, delp, pt, qv, ql, qr, qi, qs, qg, &
                 q_cond = qlz (k) + qrz (k) + qiz (k) + qsz (k) + qgz (k)
                 con_r8 = one_r8 + qvz (k) + q_cond
             else
-                con_r8 = one_r8 + qvz (k)
+                ! host keeps the input layer mass: back to specific ratios on the input basis (dp = delp*(1-qv_in))
+                con_r8 = one_r8 / (one_r8 - qv (i, k))
             endif
 
             delp (i, k) = dp (k) * con_r8
